course: dictionary
lesson: 10913
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Vocal is one of them. Vocal means about the voice or using the voice, as in «Shouting for a long time strains the vocal cords so they swell and the voice goes hoarse.»
explain: Vocal can also describe a person. A vocal person speaks out strongly and often, so they say what they think again and again. «When you hum, your vocal cords wobble» is about the voice, but a vocal neighbour who complains about litter is someone who speaks out.
explain: Vocals can also be the singing parts of a song. In music lessons, the vocals are the sung parts, not the drums or the guitar. To choose the right meaning, ask: is this sentence about the voice, about speaking out, or about singing? Then put your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Vocal means about the voice or using the voice.
fact: A vocal person speaks out strongly and often.
fact: Vocals are the singing parts of a song.
fact: Your vocal cords are in your throat, and they wobble to make sound.
fact: A vocal sac is a pouch that some male frogs fill with air to make their calls louder.
exercise: «When you hum, your vocal cords wobble as air passes them.» What are the vocal cords doing when you hum? | They hold your head still | *They wobble as air passes them | They fill with water | They digest your food
exercise: Nadia says the lead vocals were the best part of the song. What are the lead vocals? | The stage lights | The drum beat | *The singing part | The guitar tuning
exercise: Ella is vocal about litter in the park, so she writes to the council. What does vocal mean here? | About the voice | Quiet and shy | Singing loudly | *Speaks out strongly and often
test: «Male frogs fill a vocal sac with air to make their calls louder.» What is a vocal sac? | A bag of food | A type of pond | A frog's back leg | *A pouch used to make sound
test: «Shouting for a long time strains the vocal cords so the voice goes hoarse.» What does vocal mean here? | The singing part of a song | About the sea | Speaking out strongly about rights | *About the voice
exam: Jayden says vocal always means singing. Is he right? | Yes, vocal always means singing | *No, vocal can mean about the voice, speaking out, or singing | No, vocal means quiet | Yes, but only in science lessons
